 * @section le_seealso 🔍 See Also
 *
 * - @see server.js — sole consumer; owns the load-bearing call order
 *   (`PROJECT_ROOT` → `loadEnv(PROJECT_ROOT)` → `require("./lib/files-service")`)
 *   and the `/.env` + `/lib/` HTTP blocklist that keeps this module's source
 *   and the real `.env` private.
 * - @see lib/files-service.js — the request-time half of the environment
 *   contract: reads `process.env.FILES_ROOT` lazily in `resolveConfiguredRoot()`
 *   and turns a missing value into the structured `503 FILES_ROOT_MISSING`
 *   error.
 * - @see .env.example — the documented template for the two keys this module
 *   makes real (`PORT`, `FILES_ROOT`), including quoted Windows path syntax.
 * - @see package.json — declares the optional-but-present `dotenv` dependency
 *   and the `npm start` entry point that begins the boot chain.
 * - @see nginx.conf — production reverse proxy; its comment explicitly
 *   delegates `FILES_ROOT` ownership to the Node process `.env` (i.e. to this
 *   module) and its deny rules are the network layer of `.env` privacy.
 * - @see dox/main/server.dox — documents the same bootstrap from the
 *   caller's perspective, including the call-order contract and the
 *   `PORT=0` truthiness edge case downstream of this file.
